# Secrets / env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private project context for Claude Code (infra details, roadmap,
# unreleased plans) - never meant for the public repo
CLAUDE.md

# Bitwarden Secrets Manager topology (project ids, machine-account names,
# key names) - infra detail, same reasoning as CLAUDE.md above, never the
# public repo. Synced to a private backup host separately, not via git.
BITWARDEN.md

# Same reasoning as CLAUDE.md above - hardcodes real hosts/IPs/user
# choices, not app logic. Lives in the encrypted CLAUDE.md/memory backup
# pipeline instead (see CLAUDE.md "Component sub-tree" / backup section).
# The wildcard below (rather than the literal filename) is deliberate: the
# real script's name embeds an internal hostname, and this pattern still
# needs to match it on disk without spelling that name out in a public file.
/tools/bootstrap-dev-vm.sh
/tools/backup-to-*.sh
/tools/deploy-prod.sh
/tools/prod-status.sh
/tools/drive-notes.sh
/tools/backup-watchdog.sh
/tools/backup-prod-db-snapshot.sh
/tools/backup-prod-db-pull.sh
/tools/backup-prod-tree-snapshot.sh
/tools/backup-prod-tree-pull.sh
/tools/prod-tunnel-watchdog.sh
/tools/sync-graph-content.sh

# Claude Code's own working files (permission allowlists, agents, local
# scratch) - tooling config for whoever happens to be developing this, not
# part of the app. Same reasoning as CLAUDE.md above.
.claude/

# Full diagnostic graph content (structure + RU/EN text + the built
# graph.json artifact) - this used to be a plain tracked file, which meant
# `git clone` on this public repo handed out the entire product for free,
# bypassing all of the per-node auth-gated delivery work (see
# app/main.py's /api/graph/* routes). The full graph now lives in a
# separate private repo; app/graph_src/ on a maintainer's machine is a
# nested clone of that repo (its own .git, ignored here same as any other
# path under this rule), and app/static/graph.json is a local build
# artifact regenerated from it via tools/build_graph.py. A self-hoster
# cloning this repo gets the engine only, no graph.json - see
# tools/build_graph.py / README "Structure/content split" for what to
# provide instead (a trimmed demo graph is planned, not built yet).
/app/graph_src/
/app/static/graph.json

